          <li><strong>Multi-Vehicle System Design:</strong> We engineer dual-charger and load-sharing repairs that work within existing panel capacity without expensive service upgrades.</li>
          <li><strong>Close Proximity:</strong> Our 612 Jasmine Pl NW office enables rapid response to Newport addresses for both scheduled repairs and charging emergencies.</li>
          <li><strong>Code-Compliant Workmanship:</strong> Every repair is permitted through City of Issaquah or WA L&I and built to NEC Article 625 standards.</li>
          <li><strong>Straightforward Communication:</strong> We explain what your electrical system can and cannot handle, and provide honest recommendations based on actual load calculations rather than upselling unnecessary upgrades.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Our Service Process for Newport Properties</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Telephone Consultation:</strong> We gather details about your home, vehicle, charger brand, and any issues you are experiencing to plan materials and approach.</li>
          <li><strong>On-Site Assessment:</strong> Our electrician inspects your panel capacity, maps the conduit pathway, and calculates voltage drop for the planned circuit length.</li>
          <li><strong>Professional repair:</strong> We install the dedicated circuit, mount the charger, and connect all wiring with proper torque and termination methods.</li>
          <li><strong>Full-Load Testing:</strong> We connect your vehicle, verify amperage draw, check voltage stability, and confirm proper charger operation before completing the project.</li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          Call <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a> to schedule your Newport EV charging consultation. We provide clear, direct assessments tailored to your specific property and electrical configuration.
        </p>
      </div>
